he rear floor furniture, manipulating rear corner and diffuser flow with the aim of increasing aerodynamic efficiency.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Mercedes","updates":[{"component":"Rear Wing","reason":"Circuit specific - Drag Range","type":"Circuit specific","geometry":"Various winglet devices removed from rear wing","description":"Removing the rear wing winglets reduces assembly camber shedding local downforce and drag at a ratio appropriate for Vegas L/D.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"},{"component":"Front Bodywork","reason":"Circuit specific - Drag Range","type":"Circuit specific","geometry":"Mirror rear stay trim","description":"The mirror stay trim reduces local camber and loading, shedding local downforce and drag at a ratio appropriate for Vegas L/D.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"},{"component":"Rear Corner","reason":"Performance - Local Load","type":"Performance","geometry":"Rear corner winglets position and span","description":"Rear corner winglets position and span optimised around local load requirements, shedding local downforce and","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"},{"component":"Engine Cover","reason":"Cooling Range","type":"Performance","geometry":"Narrower rear exit","description":"drag at a ratio appropriate for Vegas L/D. A narrower rear exit allows more cooling range, appropriate for the lower cooling requirements of Vegas.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Red Bull Racing","updates":[{"component":"Front Wing Endplate","reason":"Performance - Local Load","type":"Performance","geometry":"Re-positioned Front Wing Endplate Dive-plane","description":"In order to better protect the flow stability of the front wing endplate footplate as well as surfaces downstream, the dive-plane has been lowered and reduced in chord length.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Ferrari","updates":[{"component":"Floor Board","reason":"Circuit specific - Drag Range","type":"Circuit specific","geometry":"vertical element","description":"The primary aim of these modifications has been to adapt to Las Vegas circuit peculiar characteristics Front floor board elements optimisation, single and car aerodynamic efficiency requirements. It is targeting aerodynamic drag saving, coming along with downforce reduction as a natural consequence, but in a favourable ratio for this track.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Williams","updates":[]},{"team":"Racing Bulls","updates":[{"component":"Floor Board","reason":"Circuit specific - Drag Range","type":"Circuit specific","geometry":"Shorter chord board elements","description":"A reduction in the amount of load generated by the Floor Board provides an improvement in overall efficiency and lap time around this circuit.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"},{"component":"Rear Corner","reason":"Circuit specific - Drag Range","type":"Circuit specific","geometry":"Modifications to drum winglets","description":"An alternative winglet arrangement on the rear brake drums delivers an efficient load reduction, providing a net performance benefit at this track.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"},{"component":"Front Wing","reason":"Circuit specific - Balance Range","type":"Circuit specific","geometry":"Reduced chord & incidence flap","description":"A low-balance front wing flap, featuring chord and incidence changes, is available for this circuit to reduce the load generated by the front wing and extend the available balance range.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Aston Martin","updates":[]},{"team":"Haas","updates":[{"component":"Rear Wing","reason":"Performance - Drag reduction","type":"Performance","geometry":"Revised rear wing arrangement associated with the Straight Mode mechanism","description":"The revised arrangement is intended to evaluate an alternative rear wing Straight Mode deployment, with associated minor changes to accommodate the different configuration.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Audi","updates":[{"component":"Rear Corner","reason":"Circuit Specific – Drag Range","type":"Circuit specific","geometry":"Updated rear brake duct deflector","description":"The revised rear brake duct deflector geometry was modified to match the specific aerodynamic efficiency requirements of the Las Vegas track.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Alpine","updates":[]},{"team":"Cadillac","updates":[]}],"sources":{"pu":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_pu_elements_used_per_driver_up_to_now.pdf","upgrades":["https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_las_vegas_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"]},"upgradesChecked":true,"parser":2}